1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
I built Benefits Intake QA to catch plan-data errors before go-live.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
When plan pages disagree, I want reviewers to see the source before loading a value.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000
On this synthetic plan, page one quotes forty-five hundred dollars individual, but only thirty-five hundred family.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The rules block it and show both lines. The family maximum cannot be lower than the individual.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Another plan has two pages and two conflicting deductibles. The result is blocked.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Individual deductible: six hundred on page one, nine hundred on page two.

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Family: twelve hundred on page one, eighteen hundred on page two. Both quotes stay visible.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
I choose both page-two quotes, then accept the other fields. The original evidence stays attached.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:57,000
After review, it becomes ready. The export keeps my nine hundred and the original six hundred.

10
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:05,000
I run fifty-six tests and a six-case synthetic evaluation. That checks regressions, not real-world accuracy.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
I publish failures too: accessibility test T-eleven fails, scans need OCR, and real-document accuracy is unmeasured.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
This earlier AI call is a genuine production archive. I made no new paid call for this video.

13
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:27,000
The AI-filled carrier stays only because it appears on page one. Rules still run first.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:36,000
This is my independent prototype: source evidence, human review, and open validation gaps before anyone adopts it.
